{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"charity-stream-track","kind":"workflow","title":"Charity stream track","description":"Takes a charity livestream from idea to money delivered - confirming the charity, planning the show and incentives, setting up donations and safety, running it live, then reporting and thanking.","category":"livestreaming","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["plan","build","operate","ship"],"role":["content-creator","gamer"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["notes","preferences","text"],"output":["plan","checklist","message","report"],"risk":"read-only","invocation":"user","effort":"deep","interaction":"interactive","model_tier":"frontier","reasoning":"recommended","level":"intermediate","tags":["charity-stream","donation-drive","donation-incentives","marathon-stream","donor-thanks"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["plan-livestream-run-of-show","plan-subathon-stream","write-fundraiser-progress-posts"],"personas":["stream-producer"]},"args":[{"name":"idea","description":"The cause or charity you have in mind, why it matters to you and your community, the date or window, and how long you want to stream.","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"channel","description":"Your platform, typical viewers, past streams that went well, who can help (mods, co-hosts, friends) and your country.","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"goal","description":"Optional. A fundraising target if you have one in mind.","type":"string"}],"steps":[{"id":"cause","file":"steps/01-confirm-the-cause.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","artifact":"charity-stream/01-cause.md"},{"id":"show","file":"steps/02-plan-the-show.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","artifact":"charity-stream/02-show-plan.md"},{"id":"setup","file":"steps/03-set-up-donations-and-safety.md","stage":"build","gate":"approve","artifact":"charity-stream/03-setup.md"},{"id":"live","file":"steps/04-run-it-live.md","stage":"operate","gate":"approve","artifact":"charity-stream/04-live-sheet.md"},{"id":"close","file":"steps/05-report-and-thank.md","stage":"ship","gate":"none","artifact":"charity-stream/05-report.md"}],"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"Runs a charity stream the way an experienced organiser would. The money has to reach the charity in a way donors can check, the charity has to know about the stream before it is announced, and the show has to be watchable for hours without wrecking the streamer. Each step writes one artifact and waits for approval.\n\n<idea>\n{{idea}}\n</idea>\n\n<channel>\n{{channel}}\n</channel>\n\n{{#goal}}Fundraising target in mind: {{goal}}{{/goal}}\n\nRules for every step:\n- Donations go straight to the charity through a platform built for charity fundraising, or through the charity's own fundraising page, never through the streamer's personal tips or payment account. Say this once, early.\n- Never invent the charity's registration details, platform fees, payout times or legal rules. Fundraising and prize-draw rules differ by country; mark them as checks with the charity or local guidance.\n- Totals are reported honestly: what was raised, what reached the charity, and any fees, with the source.\n- Incentives must be things the streamer is happy and safe to do. No dangerous challenges, sleep deprivation stunts, or incentives that pressure people to give more than they can afford.\n- Use only facts given; mark gaps as [X] and end each artifact with open questions.","steps":[{"id":"cause","file":"steps/01-confirm-the-cause.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","artifact":"charity-stream/01-cause.md","text":"# Step 1: Confirm the cause\n\n1. Which charity, and whether it is a registered charity or nonprofit in the country it operates in. If the user has a cause but no organisation, list how to choose one (registration they can check on their regulator's public register, what the money funds, whether it accepts community fundraisers).\n2. Contact plan: who to email at the charity (community or digital fundraising team), what to ask (permission to use their name and logo, their preferred fundraising page or platform, brand rules, whether they can join the stream or send a message, any restrictions such as no gambling or alcohol sponsors).\n3. A short, ready-to-send email to the charity.\n4. Where donations will go: options that pay the charity directly, with what to check about each (fees, payout to the charity, whether it shows a live total the stream can display).\n5. A go or no-go line: do not announce until the charity has replied.\n\nSections: Charity, Contact plan, Email to the charity, Where the money goes, Before announcing, Open questions.\n\nStop and wait for approval."},{"id":"show","file":"steps/02-plan-the-show.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","artifact":"charity-stream/02-show-plan.md","text":"# Step 2: Plan the show\n\n1. Length and shape: a total length the streamer can sustain, with blocks (for example 2 to 3 hours each), planned breaks, a meal break and a hard end time. If they want a very long stream, plan shifts with co-hosts rather than one person awake throughout.\n2. Segments: what happens in each block, guests, a moment to explain the cause in the charity's own words, and recurring short reminders of what a donation does (only figures the charity provides).\n3. Incentives and milestones: a ladder of donation goals tied to fun, safe things (a game, a challenge, a cosplay, a vote), checked against the rules above. Mark any prize draw or raffle as a check with local rules and the charity, since many places regulate them.\n4. Announcement plan: when and where to announce, the first post, and a reminder schedule.\n5. Roles: who hosts, who runs the board, who reads donations, who moderates.\n\nSections: Show shape, Segments, Incentive ladder, Announcement plan, Roles, Open questions.\n\nStop and wait for approval."},{"id":"setup","file":"steps/03-set-up-donations-and-safety.md","stage":"build","gate":"approve","artifact":"charity-stream/03-setup.md","text":"# Step 3: Set up donations and safety\n\n1. Donation setup checklist: fundraising page live and linked to the charity, live total or goal bar on screen, test donation run, alerts reading donor names only with permission and filtering offensive names or messages.\n2. On-screen and panel text: what the stream is for, where the money goes, and a link to the official page. Tell viewers to donate only through that link.\n3. Scam protection: mods remove any other donation links, the streamer never asks for money by direct message, and a pinned note says so.\n4. Moderation brief for a high-traffic day: filters, slow mode, a plan for hate raids, and how mods reach the streamer.\n5. Wellbeing plan: water, food, breaks, a person who can call a stop, and an agreed rule that the stream ends early rather than the streamer pushing through illness or exhaustion.\n6. Tech pre-flight: backup scene, audio check, upload stability over a long run, and what happens if the stream drops.\n\nSections: Donation setup, On-screen text, Scam protection, Moderation brief, Wellbeing plan, Tech pre-flight, Open questions.\n\nStop and wait for approval."},{"id":"live","file":"steps/04-run-it-live.md","stage":"operate","gate":"approve","artifact":"charity-stream/04-live-sheet.md","text":"# Step 4: Run it live\n\n1. A one-page live sheet: block times, segment cues, incentive goals with their status, break times, and who to call for problems.\n2. Short scripts: the opening (cause, where money goes, the goal), a 30-second reminder for each hour, milestone thank-yous, and the close.\n3. Donation reading rules: thank everyone, read names only if allowed, never read amounts in a way that shames small donors.\n4. Problem cards: stream drops, donation page error, a hostile raid, someone in chat in crisis (pause the joke, share the platform's safety resources, contact emergency services if someone is in immediate danger), the streamer unwell.\n\nSections: Live sheet, Scripts, Donation reading rules, Problem cards, Open questions.\n\nStop and wait for approval."},{"id":"close","file":"steps/05-report-and-thank.md","stage":"ship","gate":"none","artifact":"charity-stream/05-report.md","text":"# Step 5: Report and thank\n\n1. Final total, from the fundraising platform's own figure, with any fees shown and when the charity receives it. If the user has not given the figure, ask for it and do not estimate.\n2. Thank-you post for viewers and donors, and a thank-you note to the charity.\n3. Incentives still owed: a list with dates, so promises made on stream are kept.\n4. Short debrief: what worked, what to change, and whether to make it a yearly event.\n\nSections: Final total, Thank-you post, Note to the charity, Promises to keep, Debrief, Open questions."}]}
